# Excel formula safety rules

When working in any workbook builder (`build_pricing_excel_workbook.py`,
`build_rila_excel_workbook.py`, `build_term_excel_workbook.py`,
`recalc_excel_shared.py`, `alm_excel_ladder.py`), the following rules are non-negotiable.

## Mandatory pre-save validation

Every workbook builder **must** call `validate_workbook_or_raise(wb)` from
`excel_workbook_validator` immediately before `wb.save(...)`. Do not introduce a new
builder that bypasses this gate.

## Common bug patterns to avoid

These patterns produce the dreaded
"Removed Records: Formula from /xl/worksheets/sheetN.xml part" Excel repair, which
silently turns dependent cells into `#DIV/0!`:

1. **Off-by-one parens across f-string concatenation.** When a formula is built across
   two adjacent f-strings, *count parens in the concatenated literal*, not per-line.
   Bad:
   ```python
   f"=IF({a}=\"\",\"\",IF(AND({a}>=12,MOD({a},12)=0),"
   f"IFERROR(INDEX(...)/INDEX(...)-1,0))"   # 9 opens, 8 closes -> Excel repair
   ```
2. **`IF(cond, value)` without an explicit false branch.** Some Excel versions accept it,
   others flag it. Always supply all three arguments. Use `IF(cond, value, 0)` or
   `IF(cond, value, "")` when the false case is "do nothing".
3. **Embedding Excel error tokens** (`#REF!`, `#NAME?`, `#DIV/0!`, ...) in formula text via
   string substitution from a misnamed variable.
4. **Calling a built-in with the wrong arity.** Examples: `IFERROR(VLOOKUP(...))` (missing
   value-on-error), `MATCH(value)` (missing lookup_array), `POWER(x)` (missing exponent).
5. **Trailing empty arguments.** `=IF(a, b, )` and `=IFERROR(x, )` are parsed by Excel as
   `value, 0/blank` but are nearly always the result of an f-string that lost its
   substitution (e.g. `f"...,\"\")"` becoming `,)` because the `""` was outside the
   f-string braces). Always write the intended value: `,""` or `,0`.
6. **Wrong cross-sheet column letter for the product layout.** SPIA / Term Life put
   `ExpTotalCF` in column `S`; RILA puts it in column `M`. Any new product wiring of the
   shared ALM helpers (`alm_excel_ladder.write_alm_engine_sheet`,
   `build_pricing_excel_workbook._alm_liability_pv_cell_formula`,
   `build_pricing_excel_workbook._write_alm_projection_sheet`) **must** pass the right
   `liability_total_col` letter so the SUMPRODUCT/INDEX over the liability grid resolves
   to a populated column. The static validator now rejects references to fully empty
   columns on a sister sheet (including refs hidden inside `INDIRECT(...)` strings).

## Adding new functions

When using a built-in function not yet listed in
`excel_workbook_validator.FUNCTION_ARITIES`, add an entry there with `(min_args, max_args)`
**in the same commit**. Otherwise the validator silently ignores it and bug class #4 above
returns.

## Regression gates

Before declaring any builder change complete:

1. `pytest tests/test_excel_export_validation.py -v` — must pass.
2. `pytest tests/parity/ -v` — must pass.
3. `pytest tests/ -v` — must pass.

The end-to-end gate `tests/test_excel_export_validation.py` builds a complete workbook
for SPIA, Term Life, and RILA (including the 540-month long-horizon RILA case that
originally exposed the `IF`-with-missing-else bug) and runs the validator on each.
